n the Prime  Minister's deal and I hope people are  focusing on this because if you think  that through extension to article 50  which is going to be a vote which would  effectively give let's say a couple of  months extension would resolve nothing  it would put us in a world in which we  were still in a zombie world not knowing  where we're going and it would increase  the chance of other options that would  increase the chance either of people  pushing for general elections which  wouldn't solve everything for another  referendum which I think would solve  nothing at all it would just tell us  what we already know which is that the  country is divided or it would push  people towards a customs union which  would stop as being able to trade with  the rest of the world so all these other  options are worse options which is why  apart from the fact I genuinely believe  this is a positivity and it's the deal  that can really work  for the economy we need to vote for the  Prime Minister's deal but which one  would you pick  I mean the last time this was put before  Parliament the government suffered the  worst defeat of any government ever and  it's not an unreasonable question to ask  that if that is if it's defeated again  which one would you choose out of no  deal or an extension to article 15  personally I think we would have to be  forced into an extension for article 50  but I think people need to understand  that that is a worse option than the  Prime Minister's deal it's not where we  want to be it's not where I want to be I  think these are horrible options the  reason I've been trying to passionately  argue for the Prime Minister's deal from  the beginning is that I think the nearly  two years negotiations a lot of very  very talented people have come up with a  good deal and it would be ridiculous to  reject this opportunity for these  uncertain and worse futures is the  government planning to whip the vote on  knodell I don't know what the answer  that is t